<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Simancas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/939">939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Simancas was fought in August 939 near Simancas on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisuerga">Pisuerga</a>, close to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramiro-ii-of-leon">Ramiro II of León</a> and the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. The Christian forces, with Navarrese and Castilian allies, won a decisive victory, and the caliph narrowly escaped. It allowed León to resettle lands to the south, and Abd al-Rahman never again led a campaign in person.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-simancas.jpg" alt="Battle of Simancas" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fondo Antiguo de la Biblioteca de la Universidad de Sevilla from Sevilla, España · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Las_Glorias_Nacionales,_1852_%22Don_Ramiro_de_Le%C3%B3n_derrota_al_cordob%C3%A9s_junto_a_Simancas%22._(4013184561).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
